       "en": "Finally, **networking** is huge in the US. Many jobs are never posted: someone knows someone. It’s normal to **reach out** to a stranger on LinkedIn and say: “Hi Dana, I’m a hygienist who just moved to Tampa from France. Would you be open to a quick chat about the job market here?” Most people say yes and are happy to help. It’s not pushy; it’s how the system works.",
