     "text": "Five things I tell every client before an interview\n\n1. Do your homework. Spend 20 minutes on the company’s website and reviews. If you can mention something specific, like their new location or a community event, you instantly stand out.\n\n2. Prepare three stories. Most interview questions can be answered with one of three stories: a time you solved a problem, a time you worked with a difficult person, and a time you went above and beyond. Practice them out loud with the STAR method.\n\n3. Dress one step above the job. For a dental office, clean business casual is perfect, not scrubs. For retail, look like the best-dressed person on the sales floor.\n\n4. Don’t be afraid of silence. If you need a second to think, say “That’s a great question, let me think for a second.” Nobody expects instant answers.\n\n5. Send a thank-you email the same day. It takes three minutes, and many candidates skip it. A short, warm note can be the reason you get the offer instead of someone else.\n\nAnd remember: an interview is a conversation, not an exam. You are also deciding if this job is right for you.",
