       "en": "When people speak fast in a meeting, it’s **always okay to ask**. Americans prefer a question to a mistake later. Use: **“Sorry, could you say that again?”**, **“Just to clarify, do you mean… or…?”**, **“When you say ‘ASAP’, do you mean today?”**. Asking a clear question makes you look careful and professional, not weak.",
