       "en": "People are busy and emails get lost. If someone doesn’t answer in 3–5 days, it’s completely normal to send a **follow-up**. Keep it light and never blame: “**Just following up on** my email from last Tuesday about the new patient forms. Let me know if you need anything else from me!” Avoid “As I already said…” or “I’m still waiting”, which sound annoyed.",
